---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import BetaCTA from '../components/BetaCTA.astro';

const title = 'Roadmap | Sky3 Network';
const description = 'Sky3 protocol development roadmap: from the current landing page and manifesto to the full DePIN data layer, benchmarking hub, and foundation governance.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <Header />
  
  <main>
    <article>
      <div class="container narrow">
        <div class="breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <span>→</span>
          <span>Roadmap</span>
        </div>
        
        <h1>Protocol Roadmap</h1>
        
        <p class="lead">Sky3 is being built in phases. The landing page, manifesto and sample leaderboard are live today. The components below are planned for the beta and beyond.</p>
        
        <div class="status-legend">
          <div class="status-item">
            <span class="status-badge status-live">Live</span>
            <span>Available now</span>
          </div>
          <div class="status-item">
            <span class="status-badge status-planned">Planned</span>
            <span>In development or scoping</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <section class="roadmap-section">
          <div class="section-header">
            <h2>Phase 1: Landing Page & Protocol Manifesto</h2>
            <span class="status-badge status-live">Live</span>
          </div>
          
          <p>Establish credibility as a neutral standards body, build an early waiting list, and attract data contributors.</p>
          
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Landing page:</strong> hero, manifesto, sample leaderboard, and how-it-works sections.</li>
            <li><strong>Waitlist signup:</strong> data-ingestion beta registration.</li>
            <li><strong>Documentation:</strong> explanatory pages covering spatial AI, world models, metrics, and protocol glossary.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        
        <section class="roadmap-section">
          <div class="section-header">
            <h2>Phase 2: Data-Ingestion Beta</h2>
            <span class="status-badge status-planned">Planned</span>
          </div>
          
          <p>Open the first ingestion pipeline to a small group of contributors, reviewers and AI developers.</p>
          
          <h3>DePIN Data Layer</h3>
          <span class="status-badge status-planned">Planned</span>
          
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Crowdsourced ingestion pipeline:</strong> upload interface for LiDAR scans (.las, .laz, .ply), CAD files (.step, .stl, .obj), robot trajectory logs (.csv, .json), and geometry imagery.</li>
            <li><strong>Privacy and sanitization engine:</strong> automated metadata stripping, face detection and removal, and IP sanitization before data enters the archive.</li>
            <li><strong>Point incentives:</strong> reward contributors for verified, rare or complex edge cases. Points are a record of contribution during the beta; they have no monetary value, and any future use will be decided through governance.</li>
          </ul>
          
          <h3>Verification Protocol</h3>
          <span class="status-badge status-planned">Planned</span>
          
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Automated validation:</strong> file integrity checks, duplicate detection, format verification and label consistency.</li>
            <li><strong>Human-in-the-loop (HITL) review:</strong> independent reviewers will verify quality, correctness and labeling. Multiple reviewers per case, with agreement required before a case enters the benchmark.</li>
            <li><strong>Reviewer incentives:</strong> points for accurate reviews, with reputation tracking.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        
        <section class="roadmap-section">
          <div class="section-header">
            <h2>Phase 3: Benchmarking Hub & Model Evaluation</h2>
            <span class="status-badge status-planned">Planned</span>
          </div>
          
          <p>Launch the live leaderboard and model sandbox API for independent testing.</p>
          
          <h3>Model Sandbox API</h3>
          <span class="status-badge status-planned">Planned</span>
          
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Inference endpoint:</strong> AI developers submit model outputs (predicted meshes, point clouds, part labels, assembly trees) for scoring on verified held-out test splits.</li>
            <li><strong>Evaluation metrics:</strong> 2D-to-3D construction accuracy, 2D/3D bounding box IoU, structural integrity, assembly tree accuracy, and physical logic checks. Detailed metrics are defined on the <a href="/metrics">metrics page</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Result publication:</strong> scores published on the public leaderboard with links to evaluation methods and code.</li>
          </ul>
          
          <h3>Live Spatial Leaderboard</h3>
          <span class="status-badge status-planned">Planned</span>
          
          <p>Replace the current sample leaderboard with real model scores. Models ranked on verified real-world cases, not synthetic benchmarks chosen by their developers.</p>
        </section>
        
        <section class="roadmap-section">
          <div class="section-header">
            <h2>Phase 4: Decentralized Storage & Governance</h2>
            <span class="status-badge status-planned">Planned</span>
          </div>
          
          <p>Transition to decentralized infrastructure and community governance.</p>
          
          <h3>Decentralized Storage</h3>
          <span class="status-badge status-planned">Planned</span>
          
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Storage backend:</strong> evaluate Filecoin/IPFS or Arweave for large 3D asset files, CAD models and point clouds.</li>
            <li><strong>Proof-of-Validation consensus:</strong> define criteria for verification consensus, data provenance, and archive integrity.</li>
          </ul>
          
          <h3>Non-Profit Foundation & Governance</h3>
          <span class="status-badge status-planned">Planned</span>
          
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Foundation formation:</strong> establish a non-profit entity to steward the protocol, maintain infrastructure, and facilitate governance.</li>
            <li><strong>Community governance:</strong> protocol changes (metrics, verification rules, archive policies) decided through open processes with input from contributors, reviewers and model developers.</li>
            <li><strong>Point-based participation:</strong> contributors and reviewers will earn points during the beta. Any future use of points (such as governance voting) will be decided by the community, not by the foundation.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        
        <section class="roadmap-section">
          <div class="section-header">
            <h2>Future: Enterprise & Safety Certification</h2>
            <span class="status-badge status-planned">Planned</span>
          </div>
          
          <p>Long-term sustainability through optional enterprise services while keeping the core protocol free and open.</p>
          
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Enterprise dataset licensing:</strong> premium access to high-fidelity, human-verified training data for AI labs fixing model hallucinations or sim-to-real gaps.</li>
            <li><strong>Sky3 Compliance and Safety Certification:</strong> paid audits providing rigorous physical safety and reliability verification for robotics, autonomous vehicles, and industrial automation software.</li>
            <li><strong>Custom benchmarks:</strong> private evaluation suites for companies testing proprietary models on verified real-world data.</li>
          </ul>
          
          <p class="note">These services fund the protocol without charging for core access. The public leaderboard, verification protocol and evaluation code remain free and open.</p>
        </section>
        
        <section class="roadmap-section">
          <h2>What's Not on the Roadmap Yet</h2>
          
          <p>The protocol is in its early stages. Several questions remain open and will be refined through the beta:</p>
          
          <ul>
            <li>Specific metrics for temporal prediction accuracy (world models forecasting motion over time).</li>
            <li>Task-specific scoring for manipulation, navigation and assembly planning.</li>
            <li>Robustness metrics measuring performance under sensor noise, occlusion and adversarial conditions.</li>
            <li>Material property recognition (rigid, flexible, brittle, transparent).</li>
            <li>The exact form of point-based incentives and whether they transition to governance weight.</li>
          </ul>
          
          <p>These will be shaped by feedback from beta participants and the research community. All changes will be documented, versioned and decided through the governance process.</p>
        </section>
        
        <BetaCTA />
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  
  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    align-items: center;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    transition: var(--transition);
  }
  
  .breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hover);
  }
  
  article {
    padding: 120px 0;
  }
  
  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  
  .status-legend {
    display: flex;
    gap: 32px;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }
  
  .status-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  
  .status-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 6px 14px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-weight: 600;
    border: 1px solid;
  }
  
  .status-live {
    background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.15);
    color: var(--success);
    border-color: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.4);
  }
  
  .status-planned {
    background: rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.15);
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    border-color: var(--border-accent);
  }
  
  .roadmap-section {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding: 3.5rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  
  .roadmap-section:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: none;
  }
  
  .section-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  
  .section-header h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }
  
  h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  
  h3 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
  }
  
  p {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  
  ul {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding-left: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  
  li {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    padding-left: 28px;
    position: relative;
    list-style: none;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  
  li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  
  li strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  
  p a,
  li a {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: var(--transition);
  }
  
  p a:hover,
  li a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  
  .note {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    font-style: italic;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--border-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    article {
      padding: 80px 0;
    }
    
    .status-legend {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 16px;
      padding: 20px 24px;
    }
    
    .section-header {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 16px;
    }
    
    h3 {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }
</style>
